190
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:21,000
And I'm guessing we have some students, staff, and family share.

191
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
I see Atkinson's in the house.

192
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Please.

193
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
And yes, we do.

194
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
And I agree.

195
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:33,000
I was very happy to hear the gusto in the room with our seven students here sharing in

196
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
the pledge this afternoon.

197
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Tonight, I bring to all of you and our seven students.

198
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
They're fifth graders from Atkinson Academy.

199
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:51,000
They're going to share with you kind of our behavior strategy and different ways that we

200
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:54,000
help to support kids at Atkinson Academy.

201
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
We call it PAUSE.

202
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:03,000
And this whole idea kind of grew out of some ABC leadership team work that we've done over

203
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:06,000
the past summer and even just before that.

204
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:11,000
So with us tonight, I have our school counselor, Kristen Woodworth.

205
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:15,000
And Kristen's going to kind of take over from here and tell us all about it.

206
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
And then the kids will jump right in.

207
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
All right.

208
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
So our school mascot is the black bear.

209
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:25,000
And the paw or the foot of the bear represents our paws.

210
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:30,000
And that's the way that we talk about and we recognize good citizenship and character throughout

211
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
a student's day that it could occur at any point.

212
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:40,000
So like getting off the bus, in the hallways, the classroom, lunch, recess, even dismissal time.

213
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
That's how we recognize students.

214
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:48,000
And our part of PAUSE, as you can see right there, is practice kindness and respect.

215
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Always curious.

216
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Work together.

217
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Stay safe and calm.

218
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:56,000
As a school counselor, I talk about PAUSE a lot.

219
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:01,000
I refer to PAUSE a lot in my lessons, in my group work, in my individual work with students.

220
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:05,000
If I'm doing like a behavior contract, I'll talk about PAUSE.

221
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:11,000
I often ask students to think about the four parts of PAUSE and how can you use that in different situations.

222
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:17,000
A big piece of bullying prevention is thinking about the difference between like an upstander and bystander.

223
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
And how can you assert yourself?

224
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:25,000
And how can you stand up for yourself and others in ways that practice the four parts of PAUSE?

225
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Using kindness and respect, being always curious, working together, and staying safe and calm.

226
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:34,000
So today I have seven fabulous fifth grade students.

227
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:40,000
And a few of those students are going to do some skits that we did in our whole school assembly a couple weeks ago.

228
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:49,000
And they are going to act out what they did for all students and staff, which kind of was a review of what PAUSE is, why it matters.

229
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
This is our second year doing PAUSE.

230
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:57,000
And then we have some other students that are going to kind of talk about a little bit how students get nominated for PAUSE.

231
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
What that looks like, what happens when students get nominated.

232
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:07,000
So we will start with our first letter of PAUSE, which is the letter P.

233
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
All right, you guys can come on up.

234
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Come on up.

235
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Yeah.

236
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,000
There you go.

237
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:17,000
We will go through the slideshow as well, kind of what's going on.

238
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:29,000
All right, so I'm going to have, let's see, you, Jackson, you can start with PAUSE, and then we'll get into our letter P skit.

239
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:32,000
The P in PAUSE stands for Practice Kindness and Respect.

240
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Students show kindness and respect when they use kind and respectful words with others, listen to others, follow teacher's directions, and using manners.

241
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Some other kids are laughing at her. Let's help her out.

242
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Hey, that wasn't kind at all. Everyone likes different things.

243
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Are you okay, Aubrey?

244
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Yeah, I just feel upset that some kids were teasing me about my new backpack.

245
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Well, as your friend, I like any backpack that makes you happy.

246
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:04,000
How do these students show kindness and respect?

247
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Yeah, so anybody can kind of answer if they would like.

248
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,000
We want to kind of involve you and see what you notice in these skits.

249
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:17,000
This is what we did during our first whole school assembly to review our PAUSE and to help our students and staff kind of review what PAUSE is.

250
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:22,000
So anybody, feel free to kind of raise your hand and answer.

251
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Yeah.

252
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:28,000
I love how her friend said, anything that makes you happy makes me happy.

253
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
And I like it because of that. That was a wonderful comment. I love that.

254
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Oh, yeah. Absolutely.

255
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Very respectful.

256
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:37,000
All right. Let's get ready for our letter A. Jackson, go ahead.

257
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:43,000
The A in PAUSE stands for Always Curious. Students are curious when they think before they speak and act.

258
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:50,000
They try new games and equipment and they ask questions before assuming.

259
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:55,000
I think Julia might be mad at me, but I should ask how she's feeling first.

260
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Are you okay, Julia? How are you feeling?

261
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Yeah, I'm just a little upset because I need a partner for the project and no one chose me.

262
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
Thanks for asking.

263
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
I think Aubrey and Grace need one more person.

264
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
We need one more person. You can work with us.

265
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Thank you.

266
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:18,000
How do these students act tears instead of getting mad?

267
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,000
How do they act curious instead of getting mad?

268
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Well, instead of just assuming she was mad at the other student, she asked, I think I'll ask her how she's feeling.

269
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:37,000
I'm curious about her as opposed to the relationship.

270
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Yeah.

271
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:46,000
I will tell you guys that if you can actually put that into practice now and take it with you for the rest of your life, it will suit you very well.

272
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Both in married life and in professional life.

273
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Should have used my indoor voice, but yes, continue that. Yeah.

274
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:59,000
All right. And, yep. Letter W.

275
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,000
The letter W in PAW stands for Words Together.

276
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Students work together when they wait their turn, they keep their school and classroom clean, and they walk on the right side of the hallway.

277
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Oh, my gosh, Julia, are you okay? Let me help you out.

278
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Thanks for helping me.

279
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
How did these students work together?

280
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Don?

281
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:45,000
There was like no hesitation. The immediate response was, let's help this person, make sure they're okay. I thought that was really on target. That was great.

282
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:50,000
All right. Jackson, we can introduce letter S.

283
00:17:50,000 --> 00:18:02,000
The letter S in PAW stands for Stay Safe and Calm. Students stay safe and calm when they keep their hands to themselves, and they keep their body and belongings out of the bus aisle, and they use whole body listening.

284
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
There we go.

285
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
What are you doing after school today?

286
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,000
I have gymnastics. I'm going to have my snack first. What are you doing?

287
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:15,000
All right. I need everyone at a level one voice facing forward so you can hear me call the names.

288
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Guys, we should be level one right now so we can hear our names being called.

289
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
